  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Black Hawk County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Twitter Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nElection Reminders\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nHistorical Records\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Black Hawk County\nElections\n\n\n\n Track Your Absentee Ballot Go to Tracker \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Black Hawk County Elections Website\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \n Where Do I Vote?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nFind Your Sample Ballot\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nSupervisor District Information\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n 2026 Primary Election Results · Official Results\n 2026 Primary Precinct by Precinct Results · Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nFeb\n \n24\n \n \n\n Special Election - Waterloo Ward 2 Council Member Vacancy\n Special Election\n \n\n More Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Board of Supervisors to be Elected by District Beginning in 2026\n \n January 20, 2026 Black Hawk County will elect members of the Board of Supervisors by district beginning in 2026, following changes enacted in Senate File 75, which was passed by the Iowa Legislature in 2025. \n\n\n\n\n Black Hawk County Post-Election Audit Confirms Accuracy of December Election Results\n\n\n\n Post- Election Audit Perfect Match\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan a homeless person register to vote?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. Any eligible voter in Iowa may register to vote. Because many of those who are homeless have a nontraditional address they just need to provide an address or description of where they sleep the most, wherever that may be. \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nI lost my absentee ballot; can I just go vote on Election Day?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. When you go to vote, a poll worker will verify with the auditor’s office that your absentee ballot has not been returned. If it is confirmed that the auditor’s office has not received a ballot from you then you will be given a new ballot to vote there. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Black Hawk County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 1, 2026\n \n\n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n28,907\n \n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n28,529\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n23,415\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n752\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 81,603\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Black Hawk County, Iowa, Elections website at https://blackhawkcountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Black Hawk County Courthouse\n\n 316 E 5th St.\n \nWaterloo, IA 50703\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Black Hawk County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\n \nMonday through Friday \n \nContact Information\n\n Elections: (319) 833-3007\n\n Courthouse: (319) 833-3000\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Twitter Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
}
